{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlooferLand/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlooferLand/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlooferLand/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlooferLand/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlooferLand/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlooferLand/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/FlooferLand/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-17T21:02:22Z","updated_at":"2024-11-17T21:02:22Z","body":"> @jcostello Meshes or its the same for lights?\r\n\r\nSorry for the very late reply!\r\nThe LightmapGI node only looks at nodes underneath its parent, its the same for all types.\r\nI believe this was done so you could have several separate lightmaps in the same scene _(which is neat!)_\r\n\r\nFor a more in-depth explanation:\r\nThe editor calls the bake function via [_bake_select_file](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/5efd124ca10bf46df62fa2441d80589777e54a5a/editor/plugins/lightmap_gi_editor_plugin.cpp#L69) and provides either the LightmapGI or the LightmapGI's parent as the node to scan from. The bake function then calls [_find_meshes_and_lights](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/5efd124ca10bf46df62fa2441d80589777e54a5a/scene/3d/lightmap_gi.cpp#L306) which is a recursive function that gets all the children of the node thats passed into it","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2481552459/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2504356933","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99079#issuecomment-2504356933","issue_ur